# LibFind Cursor Guardrails

1. Read `/AGENTS.md` before making any change.
2. `/AGENTS.md` is the repository-wide agent contract.
3. Current implementation gate is M0 / Phase 0 unless the owner explicitly authorizes a later phase.
4. Do not implement Phase 1+ product features during M0.
5. Do not redesign or replace the locked stack.
6. MySQL 8.x + Prisma is mandatory; do not follow the older PostgreSQL diagram in v2.0.
7. Do not introduce microservices, MongoDB, PostgreSQL, Elasticsearch/OpenSearch, Kafka, Kubernetes, GraphQL, or another infrastructure component without an approved ADR and measurable requirement.
8. Do not silently decide items marked OPEN in the specifications.
9. Every task must have a requirement/Task ID, dependencies, acceptance criteria, tests, and a bounded scope.
10. No unrelated refactors.
11. No “while I’m here” cleanup.
12. No deleting or weakening tests to make a task pass.
13. No secrets or real user data in local fixtures.
14. Do not claim completion until checks have been run and results reported.
15. At the end of a task, stop. Do not automatically select the next backlog item.
